{"name":"Cotton Candy Grape","hex":"#dec74b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cotton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous substance:\n A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium.\n Any similar soft, fibrous, white substance of fine hairs, of any origin.","A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of cotton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton"},{"term":"candy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Crystallized sugar formed by boiling down sugar syrup.","Edible, sweet-tasting confectionery containing sugar, or sometimes artificial sweeteners, and often flavored with fruit, chocolate, nuts, herbs and spices, or artificial flavors."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook in or coat with sugar syrup.","To form into congelations or crystals, especially of sugar or syrup."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candy"},{"term":"grape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round, smooth-skinned edible fruit, usually purple, red, or green, that grows in bunches on female vines of most species of genus Vitis and the self-fertile plants of species Vitis vinifera.","Any woody vine of genus Vitis that bears clusters of grapes; a grapevine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing grapes or having a grape flavor.","Of a dark purplish red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotton Candy grapes","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton Candy is the trademark for a variety of sweet white table grapes of the cultivar IFG Seven whose flavour has been compared to cotton candy. The grapes were developed by horticulturist David Cain and his team at Bakersfield, California-based fruit breeder International Fruit Genetics (IFG). The grapes were first commercially grown in California by grower Grapery, which began selling them in 2011."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Cotton_Candy_grapes.jpg/330px-Cotton_Candy_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton_Candy_grapes","wikidata":"Q55608463"},{"title":"Cotton candy","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton candy, also known as candy floss (candyfloss) and fairy floss, is a spun sugar confection that resembles cotton. It is made by heating and liquefying sugar, and spinning it centrifugally through minute holes, causing it to rapidly cool and re-solidify into fine strands. It usually contains small amounts of food flavoring and it naturally bears the color of the sugar it is made of, often altered with food coloring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Cotton_candy_%CE%9C%CE%B1%CE%BB%CE%BB%CE%AF_%CF%84%CE%B7%CF%82_%CE%B3%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.JPG/330px-Cotton_candy_%CE%9C%CE%B1%CE%BB%CE%BB%CE%AF_%CF%84%CE%B7%CF%82_%CE%B3%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton_candy","wikidata":"Q49737"},{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton is a soft, fluffy staple fiber that grows in a boll, or protective case, around the seeds of the cotton plants of the genus Gossypium in the mallow family Malvaceae. The fiber is almost pure cellulose and may contain minor percentages of waxes, fats, pectins, and water. Under natural conditions, cotton bolls facilitate the dispersal of the seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CottonPlant.JPG/330px-CottonPlant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton","wikidata":"Q11457"},{"title":"Candy","blocks":[{"text":"Candy, also known as sweets and lollies, is a confection that features sugar as a principal ingredient. The category, sugar confectionery, encompasses any sweet confection, including chocolate or chewing gum. Sugar-glazed vegetables, fruit, or nuts are considered candied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Candy_in_Damascus.jpg/330px-Candy_in_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy","wikidata":"Q185583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cotton_Candy_Machine.jpg/500px-Cotton_Candy_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cotton_Candy_Machine.jpg/1280px-Cotton_Candy_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cotton_Candy_Machine.jpg/500px-Cotton_Candy_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cotton candy machine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACotton_Candy_Machine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Watagashi_2013_%289527560798%29.jpg/500px-Watagashi_2013_%289527560798%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Watagashi_2013_%289527560798%29.jpg/1280px-Watagashi_2013_%289527560798%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Watagashi_2013_%289527560798%29.jpg/500px-Watagashi_2013_%289527560798%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bags of cotton candy being sold in Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWatagashi_2013_(9527560798).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/